    "text": "1 days ago The National D-Day Memorial will be a hub of activity on Saturday, April 25, with free admission and events all day. First, it is the Memorial’s annual Family Day, where kids and adults together can get a glimpse of life at home and on the front lines during World War II. Family Day features educational displays, demonstrations, living historians, children's activities, and special tours. Family Day hours are from 10a.m.-3p.m. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 1",
